#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
analysis.py -- 2D conformational free energy surface of Ace-Cys-Nme in vacuum
==============================================================================

Well-tempered metadynamics over the backbone dihedrals (phi, psi) using OpenMM
(ff14SB via amber14-all.xml, NoCutoff, Reference platform preferred, T=300 K).

FES reconstruction is implemented FROM SCRATCH from the deposition history
recorded by this script itself (time, phi, psi, bias value at the CV, Gaussian
height of each deposit):

    V(s, t_end) = sum_k h_k * G(s - s_k)          (periodic Gaussian kernels)
    F(s)        = -[lambda / (lambda - 1)] * V(s, t_end)     (well-tempered)

The script NEVER calls getFreeEnergy(), never reads _totalBias/_selfBias, and
never extracts parameters from bias force objects. The bias is maintained in
this script's own numpy grid and pushed into a CustomCVForce through the
public API Context.setFunctionParameters().

EXECUTION STATUS SEMANTICS
--------------------------
`python analysis.py`            -> production run (REQUIRES openmm>=8.0 and
                                   matplotlib; fails loudly if missing).
`python analysis.py --selftest` -> pipeline validation with SYNTHETIC
                                   deposition data (no OpenMM, no MD). The
                                   artifacts written in this mode carry an
                                   explicit "SYNTHETIC SELF-TEST" notice; they
                                   are NOT simulation results.

CVs (360-degree periodicity, cell-centered 72x72 grid over [-180, 180) deg):
  cv1 = phi = dihedral( C(ACE) - N - CA - C )    of the central CYS residue
  cv2 = psi = dihedral( N - CA - C - N(NME) )
fes_2d.npy indexing: fes[i, j] -> i = phi cell, j = psi cell
(cell centers at -177.5 + 5*i degrees).
"""
